IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. CREATE-DATASET.

ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT OUTPUT-FILE ASSIGN TO DYNAMIC DSNAME-VAR
        ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
        ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
        FILE STATUS IS WS-FS.

DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  OUTPUT-FILE.
01  OUTPUT-RECORD                 PIC X(80).

WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-FS                         PIC XX.
01  DSNAME-VAR                    PIC X(100).

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-LOGIC.
    * 1. Set the dataset name and allocation parameters
    *    Format: 'DSN(data.set.name) NEW TRACKS SPACE(1,1) RECFM(F,B) LRECL(80)'
    STRING "DSN(USERID.DATA.DATASET) NEW TRACKS SPACE(1,1) "
           "RECFM(F,B) LRECL(80)"
           DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO DSNAME-VAR
    
    * 2. Open the file (This automatically creates it from scratch)
    OPEN OUTPUT OUTPUT-FILE
    IF WS-FS NOT = "00"
        DISPLAY "ERROR CREATING FILE. STATUS: " WS-FS
        GOBACK
    END-IF

    * 3. Write data to the newly created dataset
    MOVE "THIS DATA WAS SAVED AUTOMATICALLY FROM COBOL" TO OUTPUT-RECORD
    WRITE OUTPUT-RECORD
    
    * 4. Close the file to catalog it safely
    CLOSE OUTPUT-FILE
    
    DISPLAY "DATASET CREATED AND SAVED SUCCESSFULLY."
    GOBACK.
